Use-Case Oriented Metrics

Use-case as a normalization measure similar to LOC or FP. Like FP, the use-case is defined early in the software process, allowing it to be used for estimation before significant modeling and construction activities are initiated. The use-case is independent of programming language. The number of use-case is directly proportional to the size of the application in LOC.

